\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The Tool 10 benchmark ladder on the clean RES-human $\to $ V1-mouse split (mean per-gene Spearman), built at compile time from the committed \texttt  {results/beat\_azimuth\_v*.json} files by \texttt  {scripts/make\_figures7.py}. The orange dashed line is the same-split Rule Set 2 replication ($0.569$), the honest bar. Seven challenger variants - ridge/CNN/GNN featurizations (v1, best of the three shown), GBT on Azimuth features (v2, v3), a GBT rank ensemble (v4), a deep stack with a leaked normalization (v5, flawed and retracted), a leak-free out-of-fold deep stack (v6), and multi-assay RES+V2 training (v7) - all lose; paired bootstrap $p$-values over genes are printed inside the bars where computed. The ladder is the honest record of a benchmark we tried seven ways to break and did not.}}{15}{}\protected@file@percent }
